{
  "summary": "Introduces a named constant `Sock::MAX_WAIT_TIMEOUT` (about 24.8 days in whole seconds) for the socket wait timeout cap introduced in PR 36340, and documents the cap in `Sock::Wait()` and `WaitMany()`. In `bitcoin-cli`, it updates the `-rpcclienttimeout=0` handler to use this constant instead of a 5-year timeout and clarifies in the CLI help text that 0 corresponds to the maximum supported timeout (~24 days) rather than no timeout.",
  "problem": "PR 36340 capped socket wait timeouts to `INT_MAX` milliseconds to fix macOS `select()` overflow crashes, but left the magic number inline in `WaitMany` and undocumented in `Sock` headers. Additionally, `bitcoin-cli` documented `-rpcclienttimeout=0` as \"no timeout\" while passing an arbitrary 5-year duration that was silently clamped by the socket layer to ~24.8 days on every wait.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: Follow-up to #36340 addressing review comments from pinheadmz and winterrdog.",
    "PR description notes that the timeout cap applies to every caller of `Sock::Wait`/`WaitMany` and should be documented in Doxygen comments, while `bitcoin-cli`'s help string was inaccurate about 0 meaning no timeout."
  ],
